From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:45:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: time plain SQLite against obfsvfs in Gecko, for
 encriox's spike

Stage 2's third round asks what obfsvfs costs against plain SQLite
(encriox). GeckoViewSQLiteBench answers GeckoView:SQLite:Bench by
timing the same work in Gecko's own SQLite and mozStorage on three kinds
of database, made afresh outside the profile so that Lockstore makes no
key for them: plain with mozStorage's 32 KiB pages, plain with 8 KiB
pages, and through obfsvfs with a key of its own. The kinds go in a
different order each round, and each run reports its file's header and
whether a marker is in the clear, which checks the premise.

The spike's gate asks for it with `--ei sqlbench <rows> --ei rounds <n>`
before it opens the vault, which the bench does not need, and logs each
run as a line of JSON.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
